## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses dynamic programming fundamentals through practical string segmentation, testing understanding of both top-down memoization and bottom-up tabulation approaches.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic Programming: memoization vs. tabulation
- String matching optimization (startsWith, trie)
- Time and space trade-offs between DP approaches
- State definition and transition logic

## Code Example
```javascript
// Top-down memoized solution
function minWordSegmentsTopDown(s, dict) {
  const n = s.length;
  const memo = Array(n + 1).fill(-1);
  memo[n] = 0;

  function dfs(i) {
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    let minSegs = Infinity;
    for (const word of dict) {
      if (s.startsWith(word, i)) {
        const result = dfs(i + word.length);
        if (result !== -1) {
          minSegs = Math.min(minSegs, 1 + result);
        }
      }
    }
    memo[i] = minSegs === Infinity ? -1 : minSegs;
    return memo[i];
  }
  return dfs(0);
}

// Bottom-up tabulated solution
function minWordSegmentsBottomUp(s, dict) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array(n + 1).fill(Infinity);
  dp[n] = 0;

  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    for (const word of dict) {
      if (s.startsWith(word, i)) {
        if (dp[i + word.length] !== Infinity) {
          dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], 1 + dp[i + word.length]);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[0] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[0];
}
```

## Complexity Analysis
- **Time:** O(n × m × L) where n = |s|, m = dict size, L = avg word length. Using a Trie reduces this to O(n × L).
- **Space:** O(n) for the memo/DP array.

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to design a compact prefix-search data structure and implement tie-breaking logic using a Trie.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with terminal frequencies stored at each node
- Prefix search via traversal to the prefix end node
- DFS collection of all words in the subtree
- Sorting by frequency (descending), then lexicographic order for ties

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.freq = 0;
  }
}

class Autocomplete {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  addWord(word, freq) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    node.freq = freq;
  }

  getSuggestions(prefix, limit) {
    if (limit <= 0) return [];

    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) return [];
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }

    const results = [];
    const dfs = (currentNode, path) => {
      if (currentNode.freq > 0) {
        results.push({ word: path, freq: currentNode.freq });
      }
      for (const [char, childNode] of currentNode.children) {
        dfs(childNode, path + char);
      }
    };

    dfs(node, prefix);

    results.sort((a, b) => {
      if (b.freq !== a.freq) return b.freq - a.freq;
      return a.word.localeCompare(b.word);
    });

    return results.slice(0, limit).map(r => r.word);
  }
}
```
